{
  // Typechecks the tests whose job is a TYPE-LEVEL pin. (AWTD-908)
  //
  // The root tsconfig.json excludes `tests/**/*`, and nothing else compiled
  // the test tree: `npm run typecheck`, the `tsc --noEmit` inside predeploy,
  // and the lint-staged hook all use that same excluded config, and vitest
  // does not enable its `typecheck` option. So TypeScript errors under
  // `tests/` were reported by no gate at all.
  //
  // That is harmless for a test that asserts at runtime, and NOT harmless for
  // one whose whole mechanism is the compiler. tests/api/v1-contract.test.ts
  // pins the iOS-facing response shapes with
  // `as const satisfies ReadonlyArray<keyof T>` — a compile-time assertion
  // that nothing was compiling. It stayed green while four keys
  // (statusRole, statusOrder, statusDescription, statusCompleted) were
  // removed from V1List by AWTD-853, because the runtime half only compares
  // the sample object against EXPECTED_KEYS, and both live in the test file
  // and drifted together.
  //
  // KEPT DELIBERATELY now that tsconfig.test-tree.json covers the whole tree
  // (AWTD-916), and it is not redundant: that config works from a list of
  // EXCLUDED files, so a future cleanup could switch this file's gate off by
  // adding one line to it. This config names its files positively and cannot
  // be disabled that way. Two locks on the one test whose mechanism IS the
  // compiler.
  //
  // ADD a file here whenever its correctness depends on the compiler rather
  // than on a runtime assertion.
  //
  // `types/**/*.d.ts` is not optional: the module augmentation in
  // types/next-auth.d.ts is what gives Session.user its `id`, and without it
  // this config reports phantom errors in lib/ rather than in the test.
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "include": [
    "types/**/*.d.ts",
    "tests/api/v1-contract.test.ts"
  ],
  "exclude": ["node_modules"]
}
